      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "IMRC's operational efficiency is a primary driver of its Above Average standing. The organization manages <cite id=\"15\">55.7 months of working capital in reserve</cite>, providing a massive buffer against economic volatility. This financial stability supports a wide range of services, including <cite id=\"16\">supporting 16,300 students</cite> and building <cite id=\"17\">139 water wells</cite> in recent cycles. Their direct service model allows for a <cite id=\"18\">cost per beneficiary of just $26.11</cite>, which is considered exceptional for the humanitarian sector."
      ],
      "summary": "Indian Muslim Relief and Charities (IMRC) is a humanitarian organization dedicated to supporting the <cite id=\"1\">security, freedom, and equality of Muslims and minorities in India</cite>. Since its <cite id=\"2\">founding in 1981</cite>, the charity has developed a direct service model that addresses poverty through healthcare, education, and emergency relief. In FY2023, the organization reported <cite id=\"3\">total revenue of $13,833,809</cite>, though recent filings show a <cite id=\"4\">revenue decline to $10,004,213 in FY2024</cite>. Despite this contraction, IMRC maintains a <cite id=\"5\">perfect 100/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting high standards of accountability. The organization is <cite id=\"6\">zakat-eligible</cite>, distributing funds across <cite id=\"7\">eight specific asnaf categories</cite> including the poor and needy. Their impact is significant in scale; in 2023 alone, they <cite id=\"8\">distributed 10 million meals</cite> and <cite id=\"9\">treated 85,000 patients</cite>. By focusing on direct delivery, IMRC achieves a <cite id=\"10\">low cost of approximately $26 per beneficiary</cite>, making it an efficient choice for donors targeting the Indian subcontinent. However, the organization faces a challenging operating environment and has <cite id=\"11\">not yet documented a formal theory of change</cite> to guide its long-term strategic evolution.",
